.TH XYMONLIVE.CGI 1 "Version 4.3.31" "Xymon"
.SH NAME
xymonlive.cgi \- live browser view of Xymon status changes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "xymonlive.cgi [options]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xymonlive.cgi
serves an HTML5 dashboard that receives actual status transitions from
.BR xymond_websocket (8).
It does not poll the current status board and does not read history or
allevents files. The dashboard displays only recent changes.
.PP
The gateway keeps a bounded transition ring in memory. A newly connected or
reconnected browser receives that ring and then receives new transitions as
they happen. The browser deduplicates replayed entries by gateway generation
and sequence number.
.PP
The ring is not a durable history. It starts empty when the gateway restarts;
browsers detect the new generation and discard entries from the previous
process. No checkpoint is read or written.
.PP
The client can filter events by host, service, or message text and by event
type: status transition, disable comment, or acknowledgement comment. It keeps
up to 500 events in memory and can render 25, 50, 100, 250, or all 500 rows.
Status-message text can be hidden without removing it from client-side
filtering.
.PP
The webserver must proxy
.B $XYMONSERVERCGIURL/xymonlive-ws
to the loopback gateway. The generated Apache configuration includes guarded
proxy directives; enable the Apache proxy and proxy_wstunnel modules to use
them.
.PP
An upgrade preserves an existing locally managed xymon-apache.conf. Merge the
Xymon Live ProxyPass directives from the generated configuration into that
file when upgrading an existing installation.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP "\fB\-\-env=FILENAME\fR"
Load the Xymon environment from FILENAME.
.IP "\fB\-\-area=NAME\fR"
Load environment settings for the named area.
.IP "\fB\-\-debug\fR"
Enable debugging output.
.SH SEE ALSO
xymon(1), xymond(8), xymond_channel(8), xymond_websocket(8)